  "slug": "framework-skyrmionic-polarimetry-57b2",
  "summary": "New preprints pair high-dimensional OAM and spatially entangled photon sources with squeezed-light and microwave biphoton schemes for tailored quantum light.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the generation and control of structured, high-dimensional or nonclassical light. Three preprints address spatial or OAM degrees of freedom: 128-dimensional single-photon OAM comb states with telecom-to-520 nm sum-frequency upconversion, phase-only hologram tailoring of OAM amplitude and phase, and a brighter high-dimensional spatially entangled pair source from beam-like Type-II SPDC in BBO with ~1.45x coincidence gain. Three further preprints are theoretical proposals built on other nonclassical resources: frequency-entangled microwave biphotons from a transmon-resonator dimer, emitter scattering of squeezed vacuum for cat-cluster-state generation, and phase matching of high-order harmonics driven by coherent plus bright squeezed vacuum. The new element is the pairing of dimensionality scaling with source brightness and wavelength conversion, alongside squeezed-light and circuit-QED schemes. The previous emphasis on complete characterization is only weakly supported here.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
